      ⍝ Regression (Blake McBride, LanguageVariances.md #4, 2026-08-10):
      ⍝ (⍳0)⊃V is the only case where Pick returns the whole array to
      ⍝ which it is applied (LRM p.42); as a selective specification
      ⍝ target this must replace the named variable's entire value
      ⍝ (shape and type included, no conformance check), same as a
      ⍝ plain V←new_value -- not the ordinary per-cell selective
      ⍝ specification that every other selector uses.
      ⍝
      A←'ABCD'
      ((⍳0)⊃A)←10 20 30
      A
10 20 30

      C←5 6 7
      ((⍳0)⊃C)←(⊂1 2 3)
      C
 1 2 3 

      ⍝ ordinary (non-assignment) value use is unaffected
      (⍳0)⊃A
10 20 30

      )ERASE A
      )ERASE C

      ⍝ regression (Blake McBride, Bugs28 #30, 2026-08-11): (I⊃A)←X used
      ⍝ to assign INTO the selected item instead of replacing it whenever
      ⍝ that item was already nested (the shape of the OLD item wrongly
      ⍝ constrained the new one) -- neither IBM APL2 nor Dyalog assign
      ⍝ into a nested target, per the LRM's own Pick example. Fixed via a
      ⍝ new Value marker (set_lval_pick_slot(), Value.hh/.cc): pick()
      ⍝ still returns the old item's own cellrefs (so an OUTER selector
      ⍝ composed with Pick, e.g. (1 0/3⊃V)←X below, can still narrow them
      ⍝ in the ordinary way), but marks them as its own direct, unbroken
      ⍝ selection; the marker only survives to assign_cellrefs() when
      ⍝ nothing narrows it first, in which case the whole item is replaced
      ⍝ wholesale instead of conforming to the old item's shape.
      ⍝
      A30←0 0 0 ⋄ (2⊃A30)←1 2 3 ⋄ A30
 0  1 2 3  0 

      ⍝ item 2 is now nested (1 2 3) -- replacing it with a different
      ⍝ shape used to give LENGTH ERROR; want A30 ←→ 0 (4 5) 0
      ⍝
      (2⊃A30)←4 5 ⋄ A30
 0  4 5  0 

      ⍝ item 2 is now nested (4 5) -- replacing it with a scalar used to
      ⍝ scalar-extend into the OLD item's shape (0 7 7); want 0 7 0
      ⍝
      (2⊃A30)←7 ⋄ A30
0 7 0

      ⍝ same story for character data (APL2 LRM's own Pick example)
      ⍝
      B30←'AB' 'CD' 'EF' ⋄ (2⊃B30)←'XYZ' ⋄ B30
 AB XYZ EF 
      (2⊃B30)←'X' ⋄ B30
 AB X EF 

      ⍝ control: Pick composed with an OUTER selector still narrows the
      ⍝ old item's cellrefs in the ordinary way (the marker above is
      ⍝ dropped by compress's own fresh, narrowed result) -- unaffected.
      ⍝
      V30←1 'bc' (3 2ρι6)
      (1 0/3⊃V30)←'ABC'
      8 ⎕CR V30
┌→───────────┐
│1 ┌→─┐ ┌→──┐│
│  │bc│ ↓A 2││
│  └──┘ │B 4││
│       │C 6││
│       └+──┘│
└ϵ───────────┘

      )ERASE A30
      )ERASE B30
      )ERASE V30

      ⍝ ==================================

      )SI

      )ERASE B

